# `s += list[i]`: for all that is proven a text may come to `s`, so it goes round the loop boxed. Behind the tests of both numbers the sum stays boxed: int32s are added as int32s.
# built on doubles, each turn asked both tags, converted both numbers, and asked the sum whether it is an int32 to box it again: ten instructions more
# The list leaves the program, so that Link has seen nothing of what comes out of it (LinkTables::resultsOfReadsByKey).
# f1 = total, f3 = inner: the head of the inner loop takes the sum. Controls: f2 = less, f4 = halves: the number goes round raw, and the sum is built on doubles as ever
